cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TEMPO (Tracking, Engagement, Messaging & Participant Outreach): automated survey scheduling and participant messaging for longitudinal studies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zweben
    given-names: Danny
    affiliation: Temple University
repository-code: "https://github.com/dzweben/tempo"
url: "https://dzweben.github.io/tempo/"
abstract: >-
  TEMPO is a server for scheduled participant messaging and completion tracking in
  research studies lasting months or years. It serves studies where individual dates and
  completed forms determine what comes next. Schedules are declared as rules over
  survey-database fields. Each run reads current study data, calculates due messages,
  checks completion and previous sends, and records delivery. SMS messaging is two-way
  through the study's own phone number. The repository documents a system running
  NIH-funded longitudinal research and contains source files with a synthetic example
  schedule, without participant data or credentials.
keywords:
  - ecological momentary assessment
  - REDCap
  - research software
  - participant management
  - longitudinal studies
  - SMS
  - survey automation
  - clinical research informatics
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22925367
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-06
